{"id":"5baf15ac-8884-4fd2-8592-6fba5a03cc48","object":"chat.completion","created":1785028717,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        w = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        edges.append((w, u, v))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected')\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"}\n```","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python code for solve(case) that computes MST of mutual reachability graph. Input case has nodes, core_distance dict, distances list of [node1, node2, distance]. For each pair, compute mutual reachability = max(core[node1], core[node2], distance). Then compute MST using Kruskal's algorithm, sorting edges by mutual reachability, then by sorted node IDs (canonicalize endpoint ordering). Use deterministic union-find (path compression, union by rank). Must return dict with mst_edges (list of [node1, node2, weight]) and total_weight (sum of weights). Must raise ValueError if disconnected (i.e., cannot select n-1 edges). Use only Python standard lib. Code must be inside solve(case). We'll encode as JSON string.\n\nEdge cases: Ensure sorting stable by using tuple (-weight? no, sort by weight ascending, then by (min_endpoint, max_endpoint) ascending). Use sorted with key lambda e: (weight, min_endpoint, max_endpoint). Since node IDs are strings, string comparison is fine.\n\nImplementation plan:\n- Extract nodes list, core_dist dict, distances list.\n- Build edge list: for each (u, v, d) in distances, compute w = max(core_dist[u], core_dist[v], d). Store canonical sorted endpoints: if u<v then (u,v) else (v,u). Append (w, u, v).\n- Sort edges by (w, u, v).\n- Union-Find class with parent and rank dicts.\n- Initialize parent and rank for all nodes.\n- mst_edges = []; total = 0.\n- Iterate sorted edges, if find(u) != find(v), union, add edge to mst_edges (as [u, v, w]), total += w.\n- After loop, if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes)-1, raise ValueError(\"Graph is disconnected\").\n- Return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total}.\n\nMake sure not to mutate case. Use deepcopy? Not necessary as we only read. But to be safe we don't modify.\n\nNow produce JSON output with key \"implementation\" and value escaped Python source.\n\nWe must ensure no extra spaces or newlines except for JSON escaping. We'll write the code as a single line or with escaped newlines.\n\nLet's write the code string."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2021,"completion_tokens":928,"total_tokens":2949,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":509},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":101},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}